\description{
\code{mfrm_d_study()} applies a practical D-study projection to the
variance components from \code{\link[=mfrm_generalizability]{mfrm_generalizability()}}. It answers questions such
as "what happens to \code{G} and \code{Phi} if we use 2, 3, or 4 raters?" without
re-fitting the Rasch/MFRM model.
